  "scale_contract": "One targets unit scale. Automatic selects the first near-equal pair scale or the arithmetic mean. The placement is rescaled in its orthonormal instance frame, preserving translation and reflection signs; shear follows native frame scaling, rather than direct column normalization. Definitions, root IDs, raw attributes/text and model groups survive.",
  "calibration": {
    "predicate": "abs(a-b) <= sqrt(machine epsilon) + 2.25e-10*abs(a) + 2.25e-10*abs(b)",
    "basis": "Empirical native boundary decisions, including three scale magnitudes, adjacent doubles, zero/translated insertion and rotated/sheared placements",
    "limit": "Matches recorded decisions; does not claim the proprietary algorithm or establish all-input equality."
  },
  "mode_memory": "Fresh default is One. Preselected roots execute immediately, and accepted getter choices persist after Cancel and Undo within one registry. Independent registries keep separate defaults.",
  "numerical_limits": "Finite normalization has a rational fallback if a ratio overflows or underflows. Local tests constrain subnormal/extreme inputs; native extreme-coordinate qualification remains limited. A separate native trial at insertion coordinates 1e16 failed instance admission before reset and is not counted as a successful reset comparison.",
  "native_helper_note": "The main and first follow-up captures predate the cancellation branch. Precision and boundary captures use the corrected branch, which avoids leaking management-result status into reset snapshots.",
  "comparison_limits": "Recorded metadata and sampled geometry at absolute 1e-9 plus relative 1e-12. Native macros use SelID, not pixel picking. Local history tests do not establish native selection/history parity. No new GPU/performance measurements.",
